choice
    prompt "Select HoneyGUI APP"
    default HONEYGUI_APP_DASHBOARD
    optional
    help
      Select HoneyGUI application to build

config HONEYGUI_APP_DASHBOARD
    bool "Dashboard APP"
    help
      Enable HoneyGUI Dashboard application

endchoice

if HONEYGUI_APP_DASHBOARD

config DASHBOARD_THIRD_PARTY_NAV
    bool "Third-party navigation mirror"
    depends on WLAN
    default n
    help
      Route the dashboard screen-cast path through the third-party navigation
      mirror SDK instead of the built-in WiFi SoftAP + carplay image receiver.

      When this is enabled AND a prebuilt SDK static library is present under
      the dashboard app's third_party_nav/lib/ directory, the two screen-cast
      paths are mutually exclusive:
        * on boot the device brings up the third-party SDK's own SoftAP + mirror
          (instead of the built-in wifi SoftAP / img_rx TCP receiver), and
        * the menu enter key switches to "third_party_nav_view" (instead of
          "carplay_view").

      When disabled (or when the third_party_nav/ SDK library is absent) the
      dashboard uses the built-in WiFi SoftAP + carplay_view image-receiver
      path, and the third-party sources/static library are not compiled or
      linked at all.

rsource "dashboard/bt_ext/bt_classic/Kconfig"
endif
